  namespace_membership_cleanup.py plugin is now available
  - closes a gap left by FreeIPA's automember-rebuild command and the underlying 389-ds automember plugin: a host
  whose userclass changes (or is removed) is not automatically removed from its OLD namespace hostgroup unless the
  same modify also causes an ADD to a different target group
  - registers pre/post callbacks on host-mod: PRE detects a real userclass change and stashes the host's DN; POST
  (after the modify commits) submits a scoped automember-rebuild task (cleanup: yes) for that one host only
  - never triggers a domain-wide resync -- a manual `ipa automember-rebuild` (or a hand-built cleanup task) remains
  the only way to do a subtree-wide sweep

  IPA server install procedure
  - chmod 644 namespace_membership_cleanup.py
  - chown root:root namespace_membership_cleanup.py
  - systemctl stop ipa
  - cp -p namespace_membership_cleanup.py /usr/lib/python3.6/site-packages/ipaserver/plugins/
  - restorecon -v /usr/lib/python3.6/site-packages/ipaserver/plugins/namespace_membership_cleanup.py
  - systemctl start ipa
  - ipactl status
